  "hindi": "हे अग्नि, तुम्हें आज स्तोमों से घोड़े के समान, भद्र संकल्प के समान जो हृदय को छूता है, हम प्रसन्न करें, तुम्हारे वहनों से।",
  "english": "O Agni, may we please you today with praises, like a horse, like a good resolve that touches the heart, with your bringings.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "ṛdhyāma is taken as \"may we please, satisfy\" with tam as object; \"may we prosper\" is the other possible sense. ohaiḥ (from √vah, \"carryings, bringings\") is unclear to me and rendered literally; te \"your\" is taken with it, but te could also be \"to you\". \"that touches the heart\" renders the compound hṛdispṛśam. The comparisons aśvaṃ na and kratuṃ na bhadram are read as modifying tam.",
